WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.144 --> 00:00:03.061
(triumphant music)

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.760
- You have some ideas in
your head about what it means

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:13.063
to be a father; but now that
I'm going to be a father,

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.202
there's a lot of fear, honestly.

00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:19.619
(multiple babies crying)

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.410
- [Instructor] All right, rookie dads--

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.960
- [David] When you walk
into the classroom--

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.490
- [Instructor] Rookie dads,
now go ahead and have a seat.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.180
- It's intense.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.180
There's a lot of diapers,
crying, and we're all nervous.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.190
We don't know what to expect.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.940
- Take a good look at Nick, here.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.774
This is your Ghost of
Christmas Future, OK?

00:00:50.774 --> 00:00:51.607
(laughing)

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:53.480
These guys, last six months,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.640
is what your next six
months looks like, OK?

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.730
Helping these guys prepare
for their future as dads

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.250
is basically about providing them

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.710
with some really simple insights.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.530
Moms like facing the babies.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.200
Dads tend to turn the babies around,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.540
face the babies out into the world.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.100
We talk about how dad
is instinctively wired

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.290
to be a protector.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.840
And a simple preparation
now can dramatically change

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.280
how things happen in the future.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.520
You are going into a nesting phase, too.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.580
You are actually gonna go through

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.840
about a 33 percent drop in testosterone.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:27.874
It'll come back.

00:01:27.874 --> 00:01:28.707
(laughing)

00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:29.540
It'll come back.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.930
- There are so many things that concern me

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.580
about becoming a parent.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.230
Even things like how to
hold your baby properly,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.760
and just keeping the house up around us

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.540
and the ground underneath us.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.180
- It's hard to overstate how
pivotal the preparation is

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.743
that we have these guys do.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.160
And set her right there.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.170
Before he lets her go, I'm gonna
wrap her up like this, OK?

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.610
Quite a significant percentage
of the guys who come

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.810
to this class have never
held a baby before.

00:01:59.397 --> 00:02:03.240
- I wasn't expecting to actually
hold someone else's child.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.983
It's an immediate reality check.

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:07.552
(baby crying)

00:02:07.552 --> 00:02:09.590
- Hand on that shoulder.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.306
And then you pat him about that hard,

00:02:12.306 --> 00:02:14.199
and see if anything comes out.

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:15.032
- OK.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.220
- It's a watershed moment.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.747
This guy who's never
held a baby before says,

00:02:20.747 --> 00:02:23.313
"Wait a second, I'm doing this."

00:02:24.229 --> 00:02:25.768
- You look natural.
(baby squeals)

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.630
Before I walked into
the class as a rookie,

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:31.630
I probably would have
said that I was prepared.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.530
It was only after I took
the class that I came out

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.385
realizing, wow, I don't know anything.

00:02:35.385 --> 00:02:36.710
(laughs)

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.930
- The veteran dads really were very open

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.300
about their experiences, and passed around

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.690
their children to complete strangers.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.240
Very brave.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.330
- The best way to prepare
for your kid's future,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.610
financially or emotionally or spiritually,

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.850
is to take the time to
get your stuff together.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.400
- The buck stops with you, right?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.850
That's the role that you're
stepping into as a parent.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.760
- [Instructor] We've got this
square dance going on here;

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.839
this is kind of fun.

00:03:01.839 --> 00:03:03.332
(laughing)

00:03:03.332 --> 00:03:05.910
The last thing I do at
Boot Camp for New Dads,

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.993
is I ask a really simple question:

00:03:09.197 --> 00:03:12.527
"What are two words you want
your child to say about you

00:03:12.527 --> 00:03:13.827
"when they have a chance?"

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.580
- I hope that they would
answer that I was loving

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.733
and that I was patient.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.300
- Yeah, that's a good question.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.190
I know that it's an
opportunity to grow and be sure

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.740
that you're in a position to lead someone

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.333
to a future you feel they deserve.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:37.150
- [Voiceover] Whether you're
a rookie parent or a veteran,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.130
New York Life has you covered.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.143
Start a plan that flexes with yours.

